  "name": "sqlite-es",
  "description": "An SQLite persistence backend for the cqrs-es framework, providing robust event sourcing and CQRS infrastructure. It leverages sqlx for asynchronous database operations, supporting event stores, aggregate snapshots, and materialized view repositories. The implementation emphasizes transactional integrity and performance by utilizing SQLite's Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) mode and asynchronous task execution.",
